{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>C_syntax.Param_guards</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"arrayjit","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Ir","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"C_syntax","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Param_guards","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>Builtin parameter guards: a test seam checking builtin calls pass arguments without narrowing.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-parameter_types\"><a href=\"#val-parameter_types\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> parameter_types : \u000A  <span><span class=\"label\">key</span>:<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span>(<span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.list</span>, <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string)</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.Result.t</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The parameter types of the function <code>key</code> that a table entry's <code>definition</code> defines, read off its signature, or why there are none to guard: <a href=\"#val-a_macro\"><code>a_macro</code></a> and <a href=\"#val-not_a_function\"><code>not_a_function</code></a> for an entry that is no function, another reason for a function the guard skips.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-a_macro\"><a href=\"#val-a_macro\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> a_macro : <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The reason given for a macro.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-not_a_function\"><a href=\"#val-not_a_function\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> not_a_function : <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The reason given for an entry that names <code>key</code> nowhere as a call or a definition: a type, a constant, a header.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-prelude\"><a href=\"#val-prelude\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> prelude : <span><a href=\"../index.html#type-param_guard_dialect\">param_guard_dialect</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The helpers the guards of <a href=\"#val-guard\"><code>guard</code></a> expand to, emitted once before them.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-guard\"><a href=\"#val-guard\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> guard : \u000A  <span><a href=\"../index.html#type-param_guard_dialect\">param_guard_dialect</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span class=\"label\">key</span>:<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.list</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The macro shadowing <code>key</code>, whose parameters have these types.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-with_guards\"><a href=\"#val-with_guards\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> with_guards : \u000A  <span><span class=\"optlabel\">?guard</span>:<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.bool <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span class=\"optlabel\">?overrides</span>:<span><span>(<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string * <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string)</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.list</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span>(<span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span>)</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>with_guards ?guard ?overrides f</code> runs <code>f</code> with every kernel prelude of a backend that declares a <a href=\"../index.html#type-param_guard_dialect\"><code>param_guard_dialect</code></a> guarding the functions the kernel calls (unless <code>guard</code> is <code>false</code>), and with each <code>(key, definition)</code> of <code>overrides</code> replacing that key's definition in the backend's table -- how a test plants a defect, and shows both that it compiles unguarded and that the guards catch it. A test seam: kernels are never guarded outside it. An override naming a key the table lacks fails the prelude's assembly.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-active\"><a href=\"#val-active\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> active : \u000A  <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><span>(<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.bool * <span><span>(<span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string * <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.string)</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.list</span>)</span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.option</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>Some (guard, overrides)</code> inside <a href=\"#val-with_guards\"><code>with_guards</code></a>, <code>None</code> outside it.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-note_emitted\"><a href=\"#val-note_emitted\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> note_emitted : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.int <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.unit</span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-emitted\"><a href=\"#val-emitted\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> emitted : <span><span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"xref-unresolved\">Base</span>.int</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>How many guards the preludes assembled in this process carried: zero where no backend declares a dialect, which is how a test sees that its guards were never emitted.</p></div></div>"}